              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(remember to check the restrictions)",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-1$ or $x\\geq-\\frac12$",
          "worked": "The quadratic $y=(x+1)(2x+1)$ opens upwards and has zeroes $-1$ and $-\\frac12$. Therefore\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(2x+1)&\\geq0\\\\x&\\leq-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x\\geq-\\frac12.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe original denominator excludes $x=-1$. Hence $x<-1$ or $x\\geq-\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
